"THE SCHEDULER CLASSIFICATION (2026-07-08, the doctrine directive: functionality with a performant override must be DEFINED in the shared lambda base). system:classify_heads over the six fetched pops ⟨ruleAgg, ruleDerives, derivation, spans, constraint, ruleReads⟩ answers the passHeads rows ⟨pass, head⟩ for the five labels agg / keyed / sweep / dred / aggwhole. python engine._classify_heads is the certified-equal override (run_rules consumes it; tests/test_classify_canon.py twins the two on every run); scheduler_cells materializes the rows as the passHeads cell at compile; the rust resident reads the cell. Populations are sets: row order is the materializing host's presentation.",

DEF("system:cls_aggids",
    S3(A("COMP"), A("theta:dedup"),
       S3(A("COMP"), S2(A("ALPHA"), N(1)), N(1)))),

